      "system": {
        "slug": "me-npc-biotic-slam",
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>You seize a target with a biotic field, lift them helplessly into the air, then slam them into the ground with crushing force.</p><p>Choose a creature within <strong>30 feet</strong>. The target must attempt a @Check[fortitude|dc:resolve(13+@actor.system.details.level.value+floor(@actor.system.details.level.value/3))|options:me-power:me-npc-biotic-slam] save against the creature's power DC.</p><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> Unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes @Damage[(1*(1+floor(@actor.system.details.level.value/4)))d6[bludgeoning]] damage and is moved 5 feet in any direction.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is lifted 10 feet into the air and then slammed down, taking @Damage[(3*(1+floor(@actor.system.details.level.value/4)))d6[bludgeoning]] damage and becoming <strong>Stunned 1</strong> and <strong>Prone</strong>.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but @Damage[(6*(1+floor(@actor.system.details.level.value/4)))d6[bludgeoning]] damage, <strong>Stunned 2</strong>, and the target's movement speed is halved until the end of its next turn.</p><p><strong>Recharge</strong> The creature can't use this power again for [[/br 1d4 #Recharge]]{1d4 rounds}.</p><hr/><p><em>NPC version. Its DC is 13 + level + a third of level (the moderate DC for the creature's level), and its damage dice multiply every 4 levels. When a creature rolls the save, the result is applied automatically (see the Auto-Apply Power Effects setting).</em></p>",
          "gm": ""
        },
